<description>
Drop the moving-color objects downward until they rest above a one-row cushion before the obstacle or bottom edge.

Input structure:
- The grid has exactly three colors: empty background, a stationary obstacle/floor color, and a moving object color.
- The obstacle color is the unique non-background role that touches the bottom edge.
- Moving pixels start outside the obstacle cells, outside the row directly above each obstacle pixel, and outside the bottom row.

Rule:
- Keep the background and obstacle pixels fixed.
- Treat obstacle pixels, cells directly above obstacle pixels, and the bottom row as blocked.
- Repeatedly move every 4-connected moving-color object one row down when its translated shape does not hit blocked cells or another moving object.

Key insight: The visible floor has an invisible one-row cushion above it, so the objects fall under gravity but stop with one empty row before the floor or the grid bottom.
</description>
<annotation>
{
  "type": "move_along_path",
  "src": "4-connected objects in the moving color",
  "path": "vertical downward path through background cells until the next step would hit blocked space or another moving object",
  "dst": "settle above the one-row cushion before obstacle pixels or the bottom edge",
  "trajectory": "move all currently movable objects one row at a time simultaneously; same-color objects may stack or merge",
  "transform": "keep background and obstacle pixels fixed; obstacle pixels, cells directly above obstacle pixels, and the bottom row are blocked"
}
</annotation>
<generation_spec>
```yaml
spec:
  grid: 4-10 rows x 7-20 cols; output same size
  colors: exactly 3 — background (most frequent), obstacle (present on bottom row), moving (never on bottom row or in blocked cells)
  obstacle:
    structure: column-fill — each column is solid obstacle from some height down to bottom row
    floor_profile: 2-4 distinct heights forming a terrain; creates 1-5 pockets (contiguous column runs above min height)
    bottom_profile: bottom-heavy; usually most columns on the bottom row are obstacle, with rare sparse bottom-only post cases
    height_profile: occupied obstacle columns are low on average (about 1-3 cells); occasional taller columns may appear but must not dominate
    bottom_concentration: most obstacle pixels lie in the bottom three rows
    connectivity: 1-3 connected components (posts/walls can be separate)
    coverage: 8-52% of grid cells
  moving_objects:
    count: 1-3 per input (4-connected monochromatic components)
    size: 1-21 pixels; bbox 1-6 rows x 1-7 cols
    placement: each object fits within free (non-blocked) cells of a pocket; columns stay within pocket bounds
    initial_position: objects start in upper portion of grid, above blocked zone
    output_separation: after settling, no moving object pixel is 8-adjacent to any obstacle pixel
  blocked_zone: obstacle pixels + one-row cushion above each obstacle pixel + entire bottom row
  transform: |
    Drop all moving objects simultaneously under gravity (one row per step).
    An object moves down if its shifted shape hits no blocked cell and no other moving pixel.
    Repeat until no object can move. Objects preserve shape; columns unchanged.
    Objects may merge into fewer components after settling.
  non_triviality: at least one object drops >= 1 row; drop range 0-4 rows per object [observed]

generation_strategy:
  approach: output-first (build settled state, then lift objects to create input)
  steps:
    - "Pick grid size (H x W), 3 distinct colors for bg/obstacle/moving"
    - "Build a bottom-heavy obstacle floor profile — prefer high bottom-row coverage with mostly 1-3 cell obstacle columns; allow only occasional taller columns and rare sparse bottom-only post profiles"
    - "Compute blocked mask (obstacle + cushion + bottom row)"
    - "For each pocket, optionally place a moving object in its settled (output) position — object's bottom pixels sit one row above the first blocked row in their columns; object fits entirely in free cells; 1-3 objects total"
    - "Verify all output moving pixels are in free cells, each object cannot shift down further, and no output moving pixel is 8-adjacent to obstacle"
    - "For each object, choose a random upward shift (>= 1 for at least one object) such that the lifted object still fits in free cells and does not overlap blocked cells"
    - "Clear settled positions and stamp objects at lifted positions to get the input grid"
    - "Validate: run solver on input and confirm output matches the settled state built in step 4"
```
</generation_spec>
