  steps:
    1. Pick grid 13x13, bg=0. Choose N in {2,3}. Pick 2*N+1 distinct non-bg colors; assign 1 as base, N as source, N as replacement.
    2. Build the OUTPUT rectangle (4-7 rows x 4-7 cols) using base + replacement colors. Fill with base, then paint N connected blobs (one per replacement color, 3-5 cells each) ensuring base >= 56% of area.
    3. Derive the INPUT target by swapping each replacement color back to its source color.
    4. Place target rectangle at a random position on the 13x13 grid with >=2 cells margin from all edges (to leave room for legends).
    5. For each (replacement, source) pair, create a 1x2 legend domino [replacement, source]. Place each on the grid separated from the target and all other dominos by >=1 bg cell.
